{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"reference:125bc010806a2a31","name":"Derriphan","source":{"id":"source:reference-125bc010806a2a31","title":"Derriphan","revision":20391,"timestamp":"2024-08-25T23:45:43Z","sha256":"e0a8b4868afde1d2625ab3ab3b3a05505fcee50096465d682e77ddfe468b1804","url":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?oldid=20391","history":"https://swse.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=Derriphan&action=history"},"article":{"sourceId":"source:reference-125bc010806a2a31","blocks":[{"tag":"p","children":[{"tag":"i","children":["Reference Book: ",{"tag":"a","children":["Jedi Academy Training Manual"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Jedi_Academy_Training_Manual"}]},"\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["Many consider the Derriphan a mythical creature, while others assume it went extinct before ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Great Sith War"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Great_Sith_War"},". In truth, it still survives in the darkest corners of the galaxy. A semi-corporeal creature that is a physical manifestation of Dark Side energies, the Derriphan is thought to have originated in ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Deep Core"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Deep_Core?action=edit&redlink=1"},", near the center of the galaxy on worlds whose suns burned out eons ago. The Derriphan is, in a literal sense, ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," of ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"}," given physical form; much as ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," can influence physical sites, the Derriphan was likely once a living creature consumed by ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," and transformed.\n"]},{"tag":"p","children":["What makes the Derriphan so dangerous is its ability to temporarily convert itself fully into Dark Side energy. When it does so, the Derriphan enters the body of another creature, feeding on its life force and seizing control of its mind. Some Jedi speculate that there are far more Derriphan in the galaxy than most suspect, and that the majority of Derriphan reside within host bodies, making them impossible to detect. Since Derriphan are strongly drawn to creatures sensitive to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Force"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Force","referenceId":"reference:67fe90e919b74d0f"},", many believe that some powerful Dark Jedi were not seduced to ",{"tag":"a","children":["The Dark Side"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/The_Dark_Side"}," but rather possessed by Derriphan, though the Jedi Council dismisses this theory as little more than an excuse to defend the Dark Jedi against their own actions.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h3","children":["Derriphan Encounters"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Derriphan are rarely encountered openly, at least initially. It is more likely that a Derriphan will reveal itself after casting off its host. Perhaps a ",{"tag":"a","children":["Sith Apprentice"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Sith_Apprentice","referenceId":"reference:580167d0bdd39739"}," opposed to the heroes is actually under the control of a Derriphan, and once the Derriphan is defeated, the apprentice is free of its Dark Side influence. If and when a Derriphan possesses a hero, the Gamemaster should consult with the player of that character to determine how to proceed. If the player is willing, the Derriphan-possessed hero could work against the other heroes in secret, either for a short while or throughout the rest of the campaign.\n"]},"\n",{"tag":"h2","children":["Derriphan Statistics (CL 7)"]},"\n",{"tag":"h4","children":["Normal"]},"\n",{"tag":"p","children":["Tiny Airborne ",{"tag":"a","children":["Beast"],"href":"https://swse.miraheze.org/wiki/Beast","referenceId":"reference:628bf77a740094a9"}," 8\n"]},{"t